    <p class="block-intro">Suspects that were run and behaved correctly.</p>
    <ul class="plain">{checked_html}</ul>
  </section>

  {'<section id="unverified"><h2>Suspected, not reproduced</h2><p class="block-intro">Seen while reading code but not run, or run without a result. Not counted above and not to be treated as confirmed.</p><ul class="plain">' + unverified_html + '</ul></section>' if unverified else ''}

  <section id="method">
    <h2>How this was tested</h2>
    <div class="twocol">
      <div>
        <h3>Live server</h3>
        <p>Orders, stock, fulfillment and returns were driven over HTTP against a running API server with four workers, a real task worker, Postgres and the sample shop data. Test products were created per scenario; every action under test went through the public GraphQL API as a staff user. Simultaneous cases fired two requests at the same instant, five to eight times each.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Isolated tests</h3>
        <p>Payments, background tasks and most webhook cases run as tests on the project's own fixtures and real database, with a local HTTP receiver where delivery matters. A few timing problems in background jobs were shown by pausing one run at a fixed point instead of racing; those entries say so.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Limits</h3>
        <p>The dashboard itself was not exercised, so whether its screens expose each API-level problem is not known. Entries marked as needing a wrong ID or unusual input were only shown through the API. Timings come from one development machine.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Re-running</h3>
        <p>All scripts are in <code>_repro/</code> at the repository root. Each prints or asserts the faulty outcome.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre>
# live scenarios (need the API server and worker running in the container)
.worktree-container/compose.sh exec -T saleor /app/_repro/orders/run.sh 07_double_draft_complete.py

# isolated tests (pass when the problem is present)
.worktree-container/compose.sh exec -T -e DATABASE_URL=postgres://saleor:saleor@db/saleor_wh saleor \\
  pytest --reuse-db -n0 -p no:cacheprovider _repro/webhooks/ -q</pre>
  </section>
</div>
"""

out = os.path.join(HERE, "backoffice-problem-register.html")
with open(out, "w") as f:
    f.write(PAGE)
print(out, total, counts)

